CORE
upward_name_referencing1.sv
--bound 5
^\[top\.cons\.p_ok\] always top\.cons\.probe == top\.prod\.cnt: PROVED up to bound 5$
^\[top\.cons\.p_bad\] always top\.cons\.probe == 0: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Upward name referencing (1800-2017 23.8): the consumer instance reads a
signal in the sibling producer instance by going up through the
top-level module name (top.prod.cnt). The reference must resolve to the
sibling's counter, so p_ok holds and p_bad (probe constantly zero) is
refuted.
